      "description": "Disabled raw intensity image + retained CameraInfo rectification template. Prime calibration before images. Full unbinned monocular CameraInfo only; R may be nonidentity but P must have zero translation. The rectifier changes pixel coordinates and names a new optical frame, returning the explicit raw-to-rectified rotation. It does not transform axial depth or perform stereo/robot calibration. Image acquisition stamps are retained; original calibration and binding provenance remain in Info. All live endpoints stay disabled; no simulator or robot is launched.",
